IS  - 2398-6352 (Linking)
VI  - 5
IP  - 1
DP  - 2022 Jan 27
TI  - Deploying digital health tools within large, complex health systems: key 
      considerations for adoption and implementation.
PG  - 13
LID - 10.1038/s41746-022-00557-1 [doi]
LID - 13
AB  - In recent years, the number of digital health tools with the potential to 
      significantly improve delivery of healthcare services has grown tremendously. 
      However, the use of these tools in large, complex health systems remains 
      comparatively limited. The adoption and implementation of digital health tools at 
      an enterprise level is a challenge; few strategies exist to help tools cross the 
      chasm from clinical validation to integration within the workflows of a large 
      health system. Many previously proposed frameworks for digital health 
      implementation are difficult to operationalize in these dynamic organizations. In 
      this piece, we put forth nine dimensions along which clinically validated digital 
      health tools should be examined by health systems prior to adoption, and propose 
      strategies for selecting digital health tools and planning for implementation in 
      this setting. By evaluating prospective tools along these dimensions, health 
      systems can evaluate which existing digital health solutions are worthy of 
      adoption, ensure they have sufficient resources for deployment and long-term use, 
      and devise a strategic plan for implementation.
