DP  - 2025 Aug 7
TI  - Bringing Interoperability into Action: Adoption of Health Terminology Standard in 
      Indonesia.
PG  - 83-87
LID - 10.3233/SHTI250806 [doi]
AB  - Achieving semantic interoperability using terminology standards is essential to 
      ensure consistent meaning of data while it is being exchanged. This study 
      examines the adoption of international and local health terminology standards in 
      Indonesia's national health information exchange (HIE) platform called SATUSEHAT. 
      The platform uses SNOMED CT, LOINC, ICD-10, and ICD-9 CM, alongside local 
      terminology standards. Analysis across five use cases using published 
      interoperability implementation guides reveals SNOMED CT domination in clinical 
      data, LOINC for laboratory data, and significant adoption of local terminology 
      standards. These findings underline the challenge of local context adaptation 
      while using the international terminology standards. Future study using 
      real-world data in SATUSEHAT platform is essential to understand the level of 
      adoption and interoperability in Indonesia.
