TI  - Strengthening digital health equity by balancing techno-optimism and 
      techno-skepticism through implementation science.
PG  - 203
LID - 10.1038/s41746-023-00954-0 [doi]
LID - 203
AB  - As result of the pandemic-related increase in telehealth and the 21st Century 
      Cures Act, technology is playing an increasing role in healthcare. This has led 
      to organizational investments in the “digital front door” of healthcare. The 
      promise that these technologies can revolutionize care by better connecting us to 
      our patients, overcoming analog barriers to care, and addressing health 
      disparities is grounded in “techno-optimism.” We advocate for organizational 
      leaders to inform their digital health equity strategies with a balanced measure 
      of “techno-skepticism”, grounded in implementation science, that can ensure 
      alignment between health technology and health equity.
