TI  - Acceptance of Digital Health Services in Emergency Medical Services in North 
      Greece.
PG  - 434-435
LID - 10.3233/SHTI250373 [doi]
AB  - This study explores the acceptance of digital health services among Emergency 
      Medical Services (EMS) professionals in Northern Greece using the Technology 
      Acceptance Model (TAM). Data from eighty-two (82) participants revealed a 
      generally positive attitude towards digital transformation, emphasizing the need 
      for further training in digital literacy. Key findings suggest that perceived 
      usefulness (PU) and ease of use (PEOU) are critical drivers for the adoption of 
      digital health technologies.
