TI  - Assessing the Fidelity of Electronic Health Record Implementation Using SatuSehat 
      Platform in Indonesia.
PG  - 1614-1615
LID - 10.3233/SHTI251128 [doi]
AB  - Indonesia's Ministry of Health launched the SatuSehat platform in 2022 to unify 
      Electronic Health Record (EHR) data and improve interoperability nationwide. By 
      December 2024, all healthcare providers were required to submit encounter and 
      diagnosis data. This study analyzed dashboard data from 33,901 facilities to 
      assess submission fidelity. In October, 58% met the 50% threshold, but rates 
      declined by December when the target increased to 100%. Findings highlight 
      disparities across facility types and regions, underscoring the need for targeted 
      support, stronger monitoring, and strategies to ensure sustainable EHR adoption.
