TI  - Variation In Rural Health Information Technology Adoption And Use.
PG  - 365-70
LID - 10.1377/hlthaff.2015.0861 [doi]
AB  - While rural hospitals and physicians have adopted health information technology 
      at the same, or greater, rates as their urban counterparts, meaningful-use 
      attestation varies dramatically among rural providers. Also, rural providers are 
      more likely to skip a year of declaring that they have met meaningful-use 
      requirements, putting them at a financial disadvantage compared to urban 
      providers.
