TI  - CM-SHARE: Development, Integration, and Adoption of an Electronic Health 
      Record-Linked Digital Health Solution to Support Care for Diabetes in Primary 
      Care.
PG  - 338-346
LID - 10.2337/cd18-0057 [doi]
AB  - IN BRIEF Chronic conditions such as diabetes are largely managed by primary care 
      providers (PCPs), with significant patient self-management. This article 
      describes the development, pilot testing, and fine-tuning of a Web-based digital 
      health solution to help PCPs manage patients with cardiometabolic diseases during 
      routine office encounters. It shows that such products can be successfully 
      integrated into primary care settings when they address important unmet needs and 
      are developed with input from end-users.
