BTI - Health Information Technology Adoption and Utilization in Long-Term and 
      Post-Acute Care Settings
AB  - This paper provides an overview of Health Information Technology (HIT) adoption 
      and utilization in long-term and post-acute care (LTPAC) settings. This study 
      found that LTPAC have adopted electronic health records (EHRs) to support 
      clinical and business needs. Interoperable exchange of health information however 
      is not routine or widely used. LTPAC providers utilize their EHR, but 
      modernization remain slow without focused policy levers. Despite barriers, there 
      are opportunities for emerging policies to support interoperability in LTPAC.
