TI  - HeXEHRS: Design and Implementation of a FHIR-Based Cloud EHR and Client for 
      Depopulated Regions with AI and Digital-Twin Integration.
PG  - 1601-1602
LID - 10.3233/SHTI260491 [doi]
AB  - Japan's national initiative for scientific infrastructure emphasizes equitable 
      healthcare delivery in depopulated regions facing rapid aging and physician 
      shortages. To address these challenges, we developed HeXEHRS, a cloud-based 
      electronic health record (EHR) platform built on HL7 FHIR (R4) and aligned with 
      JP Core profiles, serving as a reference implementation for Japanese clinics. 
      HeXEHRS consists of a production-grade FHIR cloud server with native JP Core 
      validation and terminology services and a standards-compliant client implemented 
      with Svelte, supporting registration, documentation, ordering, and scheduling 
      workflows. Integrated AI and digital-twin connectors enable summarization, speech 
      recognition, and PHR integration. While prioritizing Japan's underserved areas, 
      the architecture is applicable to clinics nationwide and offers a globally 
      applicable approach to extend sustainable, interoperable healthcare services in 
      remote or resource-limited regions worldwide.
