TI  - Digital health and COVID-19: challenges of use and implementation in sub-Saharan 
      Africa.
PG  - 240
LID - 10.11604/pamj.2021.38.240.27948 [doi]
LID - 240
AB  - COVID-19 is a global health emergency that exposed the gaps in health systems 
      globally, especially in sub-Saharan Africa home to many fragile healthcare 
      systems and a region beset with a large burden of disease. Various mitigation 
      strategies have been put in place to stop the spread of COVID-19 and management 
      of patients in sub-Saharan Africa. However, much still need to be done. Digital 
      health provides the promise for the continent to bridge the gap in decreasing the 
      negative impact of COVID-19 and effectively mitigate the pandemic. This 
      commentary argues how countries in sub-Saharan Africa need to embrace the use of 
      digital health in public health interventions to vigorously mitigate the COVID-19 
      pandemic and to contribute towards attaining universal health coverage (UHC).
