TI  - What's Next for Modernizing Gender, Sex, and Sexual Orientation Terminology in 
      Digital Health Systems? Viewpoint on Research and Implementation Priorities.
PG  - e46773
LID - 10.2196/46773 [doi]
LID - e46773
AB  - In 2021, Canada Health Infoway and the University of Victoria's Gender, Sex, and 
      Sexual Orientation Research Team hosted a series of discussions to successfully 
      and safely modernize gender, sex, and sexual orientation information practices 
      within digital health systems. Five main topic areas were covered: (1) 
      terminology standards; (2) digital health and electronic health record functions; 
      (3) policy and practice implications; (4) primary care settings; and (5) acute 
      and tertiary care settings. In this viewpoint paper, we provide priorities for 
      future research and implementation projects and recommendations that emerged from 
      these discussions.
