TI  - Using High-Technology Simulators to Prepare Anesthesia Providers Before 
      Implementation of a New Electronic Health Record Module: A Technical Report.
PG  - 1815-1819
LID - 10.1213/ANE.0000000000001775 [doi]
AB  - Learning to use a new electronic anesthesia information management system can be 
      challenging. Documenting anesthetic events, medication administration, and airway 
      management in an unfamiliar system while simultaneously caring for a patient with 
      the vigilance required for safe anesthesia can be distracting and risky. This 
      technical report describes a vendor-agnostic approach to training using a 
      high-technology manikin in a simulated clinical scenario. Training was feasible 
      and valued by participants but required a combination of electronic and manual 
      components. Further exploration may reveal simulated patient care training that 
      provides the greatest benefit to participants as well as feedback to inform 
      electronic health record improvements.
