TI  - Rapid-Cycle Implementation of a Multi-Organization Registry for Heart Failure 
      with Preserved Ejection Fraction Using Health Information Exchange Standards.
PG  - 1560-1561
LID - 10.3233/SHTI190534 [doi]
AB  - Constructing multi-site specialty registries typically proves time-consuming. 
      Electronic health record (EHR) data collected during clinical care affords a 
      pragmatic approach to accelerating registry implementation. Heart failure with 
      preserved ejection fraction (HFpEF) is an increasingly common and morbid 
      condition. Building a multi-site registry for HFpEF proved feasible using EHR 
      data coded in standard terminologies (SNOMED CT, LOINC) and shared via Health 
      Information Exchanges.
