TI  - Implementation of an interruptive electronic health record alert improves optimal 
      antibiotic prescribing in ambulatory patients with acute bacterial sinusitis: a 
      quasi-experiment.
PG  - e24
LID - 10.1017/ash.2025.10283 [doi]
LID - e24
AB  - Sinusitis is a leading cause for outpatient antibiotics. An interruptive 
      electronic health record alert was implemented to promote optimal antibiotic 
      selection and duration for acute bacterial sinusitis when suboptimal treatment is 
      ordered. After implementation, optimal antibiotic prescribing significantly 
      increased 7% preintervention versus 30% postintervention, (unadjOR, 5.69; 95% CI, 
      2.36 - 13.72; P < .001).
