TI  - Addressing barriers in comprehensiveness, accessibility, reusability, 
      interoperability and reproducibility of computational models in systems biology.
LID - 10.1093/bib/bbac212 [doi]
LID - bbac212
AB  - Computational models are often employed in systems biology to study the dynamic 
      behaviours of complex systems. With the rise in the number of computational 
      models, finding ways to improve the reusability of these models and their ability 
      to reproduce virtual experiments becomes critical. Correct and effective model 
      annotation in community-supported and standardised formats is necessary for this 
      improvement. Here, we present recent efforts toward a common framework for 
      annotated, accessible, reproducible and interoperable computational models in 
      biology, and discuss key challenges of the field.
