OAB - For the successful development and implementation of eHealth interventions in 
      insurance medicine and rehabilitation, the needs, expectations, facilitators, and 
      barriers that physicians indicate should be taken into account.Insurance 
      physicians support the use of eHealth interventions to collect medical 
      information more effectively and efficiently, to contribute to and maintain the 
      quality of care, in the perspective of managing expected shortages in insurance 
      physicians.When concretizing eHealth interventions for rehabilitation 
      professionals, one should take the importance of face to face interaction with 
      patients into account.Extra education and training for older insurance physicians 
      may improve the implementation of eHealth interventions, because they are less 
      inclined to see its value and feel less competent to use it.
