TI  - Exploring the User Engagement Scale Short Form as a Determinant of Adherence in 
      Digital Health Interventions.
PG  - 1901-1902
LID - 10.3233/SHTI190704 [doi]
AB  - Adherence determines the impact of digital health interventions. Standard tools 
      provide a measure for user experience and predict adherence. We evaluated the 
      User Engagement Scale Short Form (UES-SF) during the POEmaS project, a randomized 
      clinical trial of an online weight loss platform. We received answers from 178 
      participants (13.7% of the cohort) and correlated the UES-SF scores with the 
      number of sessions attended. Our findings suggest the UES-SF is an accurate 
      evaluation of user experience, but only one domain (reward) was associated with 
      long-term use.
