OAB - Main findings: After the implementation of the locally developed T1 diabetes EMR 
      system, there was a significant increase in clinical attendance, data 
      completeness, reduction in HbA1c levels, and higher screening rates for 
      diabetes-related complications.Added knowledge: Demonstrates the effectiveness of 
      the T1 diabetes EMR system in improving clinical attendance, data quality, and 
      diabetes management while identifying areas needing further improvement, such as 
      systolic BP management and glucometer access.Global health impact for policy and 
      action: Informs policymakers on the benefits of EMR systems for enhancing 
      diabetes care, supports patient monitoring, and helps identify treatment and care 
      gaps to improve health outcomes.
